//! 🧬️ Iso16757 artifact — document mutation dispatch. Semantic vocabulary derived from
//! `📸️snapshot/🦀️component.rs`'s `Iso16757Snapshot` shape (catalogue/dictionary/geometry/
//! selection/part-number-rule/part-number-inputs/script-limits/exchange-process) per
//! `.🦑️repo/🎫️tickets/🎆️26/🌙️08/☀️12/SEMANTIC-MUTATIONS-OVERHAUL/📓️taxonomy.md`/
//! `📓️derivation-rules.md`. `impl protocol::Mutation`/`SemanticMutation` below are generated by
//! `#[derive(dsl::Mutations)]` — never hand-written.
//!
//! This is a rich, multi-collection document schema; this pass covers document-root scalars
//! (exchange process, script limits, part-number rule/inputs, selection facet), catalogue identity
//! (catalogue/manufacturer naming), and full create/delete(+rename) coverage for the catalogue's two
//! most central id-keyed collections (`product_groups`, `products`) plus `property_definitions` and
//! the dictionary's `subjects`. Deliberately deferred to a follow-up ticket (same recipe, more triad
//! leaves): `product_classes`, `product_series`, `product_indexes`, `descriptive_objects`,
//! `accessories`/`compositions` edges, dictionary `relationships`/`properties`/`controlled_lists`/
//! `meta_subjects`, and `geometry` (objects + primitive registry) — see this ticket's wave2 report.
//!
//! Every triad leaf is mounted directly as a `mutations`-sibling module in `📦️glue.rs` (this lane's
//! agent owns `📦️glue.rs`, so no self-wiring `#[path = "."]` blocks are needed for the TRIADS — the orphaned
//! `📄set-snapshot` stub is deleted along with its dangling glue mount).

